<resources>
    <!--
      The native half of the theme. These must track src/theme/colors.ts.

      `app_background` is `bg` — the colour of the window behind React, so it is
      what shows during an activity transition. `bootsplash_background` is
      `splashTop`, which the JS splash paints over.

      **The two are not the same value in light mode.** The v4 design draws its
      splash on a warmer cream (#FDF7EA) than the screens behind it (#FBF8F3),
      so `splashTop` is `palette.cream75` and `bg` is `palette.cream50`. Keep
      them apart: setting bootsplash_background back to the field colour
      reintroduces the seam at the top of the screen that
      scripts/check-splash-colour.sh exists to catch. In dark they still
      coincide, at palette.brown950.

      values-night/ carries the dark pair. Note what that can and cannot do: the
      OS night setting is the only signal available before React starts, so these
      follow the *device*, not the app's Light/Dark/System preference — which
      lives in MMKV and cannot be read this early. A user who forces Light on a
      dark device therefore gets a dark splash and a light app. That mismatch is
      one frame at the handoff; the alternative was a cream flash on every dark
      cold start, which is worse and was the previous behaviour.
    -->
    <color name="app_background">#FBF8F3</color>
    <color name="bootsplash_background">#FDF7EA</color>
</resources>
